# AI_Creature_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Ecological/fauna AI systems (survival_crafting).

## 2. This document owns
- Creature ecological roles: predator/prey/scavenger intents, habitat, activity cycles.
- Creature interaction rules: taming, domestication, pack logic summary, aggression triggers.
- Ecosystem balance intent (population relationships, cascade risks).

## 3. This document does NOT own
- AI implementation — AI_Systems.
- Combat stats — balance/stat authority docs.
- Taming economy outputs — Resource (linked).

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Ecosystem philosophy / 2. Species roster & roles / 3. Habitats & cycles / 4. Interaction rules / 5. Taming & domestication / 6. Aggression model / 7. Population balance / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Creature vs Enemy: ecosystem actors here; hostile combat roster in Enemy (overlap declared).
- Behavior summaries reference AI archetypes; parameters live with the archetype.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every species declares habitat, diet role and one counter (predator or weakness).
- Taming rules state output links; no inline economy numbers.
